<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Sign in · Learning Book Builder</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css">
</head>
<body class="login-body">
<main class="login-shell">
  <section class="login-copy">
    <div class="kicker">Learning Book Builder</div>
    <h1>Turn notes into routed learning books.</h1>
    <p>Upload PDFs and paste long text. The builder uses the learning-book-site skill, generates one bilingual book, and publishes it at a URL — no downloads.</p>
    <ul class="checks">
      <li>Admin-managed users, no public sign-up</li>
      <li>Daily creation quota per user</li>
      <li>Server key or bring your own model key</li>
      <li>Catalog-first reuse before generation</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <form class="login-card" method="post" action="/login">
    <h2>Sign in</h2>
    <p class="muted">Use the account the administrator created for you.</p>
    <% if (error) { %><div class="inline-err"><%= error %></div><% } %>
    <input type="hidden" name="next" value="<%= next %>">
    <label>Email</label>
    <input name="email" type="email" value="<%= email %>" required autocomplete="username">
    <label>Password</label>
    <input name="password" type="password" required autocomplete="current-password">
    <button class="btn primary wide" type="submit">Sign in</button>
    <small>No public sign-up. Ask the administrator for an account.</small>
    <% if (dev) { %><small class="dev">Development login: admin@example.com / admin1234</small><% } %>
  </form>
</main>
</body>
</html>
